      "content": "yeah exactly. it's like the only way to actually balance the scales. i'm finding that most historians agree that the era of intense union activity was basically the golden age for democracy because it forced the government to listen to the people instead of just big business. do you think there's really much left to debate about how essential they were for a fair society?",
